      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community takes its name from Samuel Parkman, an official of the Connecticut Land Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkman%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office has operated in Parkman continuously since 1806, one of the oldest in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkman%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town lies at the crossroads of State Route 422 and State Routes 88, 168, and 528, a historic junction for local travel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
